    "description": "The LG LW6017R is one of the most common small window units in the country, and for good reason. It is a 6,000 BTU, 115-volt air conditioner with electronic controls, a remote and a timer, in a compact box that fits most standard double-hung windows. LG positions it for rooms of roughly 250 square feet, which makes it the sensible upgrade when a 5,000 BTU unit runs constantly in a sunny bedroom or a small home office full of electronics. It uses a conventional fixed-speed compressor, so expect it to cycle on and off with an audible start each time, and to be noticeably louder than the Midea inverter. That also means a sharper startup surge if you run it from a generator or power station. For a renter who wants a no-surprises unit with a remote and enough capacity for a typical bedroom, it is a reliable choice."
