      "Low running watts suit a power station or small generator",
      "Standard 115V plug"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "No remote or timer",
      "Fixed-speed compressor is noticeably loud",
      "Only enough for a small room"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "For a small bedroom, dorm or office, a basic 5,000 BTU mechanical unit is all you need, and this is a good one.",
    "description": "The Midea EasyCool 5,000 BTU unit is the archetypal miniature window AC: a small box with two rotary knobs, one for mode and fan, one for the thermostat. Midea rates it for rooms of about 150 square feet, which covers a small bedroom, a dorm room or a home office. There is no remote, no app and no timer, and that simplicity is part of the appeal: nothing to configure, and a unit that restarts in its last setting after a power cut because the knobs never moved. It is light enough for one person to lift into a window, and its modest running draw makes it one of the easier units to run from a portable power station or a small inverter generator. The trade-off is noise and efficiency. A fixed-speed compressor starts and stops audibly, and it will not match the inverter Midea on comfort. For a tight budget and a small room, it is hard to beat."
